  "fromId": "t_pharyngealized",
  "toId": "t",
  "preamble": "Loss of pharyngealization (de-emphaticization): [tˤ] merges with plain [t]. Arabic and Hebrew ṭ (from Proto-Semitic *ṭ, reconstructed as ejective *tʼ) lost its secondary articulation in Maltese, Cypriot Maronite Arabic and the Ashkenazi, Sephardi and Israeli Hebrew traditions, all languages in heavy contact with European ones. In Maltese the lost contrast left traces in vowel quality (Puech 2018).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Depharyngealization, Merger, De-emphaticization",
